<details class="panel"><summary>How the list is prioritised</summary><p>Overdue references first, then due today, follow-up prompts and source checks; earliest reference date first, then apprentice reference. Filters show only their matching reasons. Counts describe apprentices, not a combined score.</p><p>Training/review flags require a sourced Active programme status. Unknown status is a source check; paused/completed/withdrawn/transferred profiles do not receive historic training overdue flags. New permitted non-private help/achievement requests still appear.</p><p>Attendance uses saved completed sessions in the last six full calendar weeks plus this week. Two consecutive completed weeks with missed sessions and no attended or unmarked sessions create a follow-up reference. Holiday, sickness and kept-at-work count as missed under the existing register definition; this is not a misconduct finding. Other missed sessions in the last 14 days are follow-up prompts. Missing/invalid registers are checks, not absence.</p><p>Task marking uses the existing seven-day reference. Task/action dates must be recorded; blocked due tasks are plan checks. Linked task actions are not duplicated. Review dates come only from checked signed-copy history. No dated task approval for at least 30 days is a progress conversation prompt where incomplete allocated tasks and reliable programme/start/decision dates exist; it does not prove no learning occurred.</p><p>Mentors see review follow-up and permitted employer-help requests; main-training detail requires main-tutor/management permission. Private help is never included here.</p></details>
